<title>UK: Indonesian 1997/98 coffee output seen at 500,000 T.</title>
<headline>Indonesian 1997/98 coffee output seen at 500,000 T.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's coffee production is expected to reach 500,000 tonnes in 1997/98 (Oct/Sept) from an estimated 480,000 in 1996/97, an Indonesian official said on Friday.</p>
<p>Oesman Soedargo, chairman of the Association of Indonesian Coffee Exporters, told Reuters annual domestic consumption was expected to remain at 120,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Soedargo is an Indonesian delegate at a London meeting of the Association of Coffee Producing Countries (ACPC).</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
